# Separation logic

{pause}
## Hoare logic + pointers

{pause}
[Hoare logic](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hoare_logic) makes it possible to verify
the correctness of imperative programs.

{pause up}
### A Hoare logic example

{carousel change-page=~n:all}
> ```ada
> …
>    X : Integer := Foo (…);
>    Y : Integer := Bar (…);
> begin
>    declare
>       Tmp : Integer;
>    begin
>       Tmp := X;
>       X := Y;
>       Y := Tmp;
>    end;
> …
> ```
>
> {style="font-size:30px"}
> ```ada
> …
>    X : Integer := Foo (…);
>    Y : Integer := Bar (…);
>
>    X0 : constant Integer := X with Ghost;
>    Y0 : constant Integer := Y with Ghost;
> begin
>    declare
>       Tmp : Integer;
>    begin
>       Tmp := X;
>       X := Y;
>       Y := Tmp;
>    end;
>
>    pragma Assert (X = Y0);
>    pragma Assert (Y = X0);
> …
> ```
> 
> {style="font-size:28px"}
> ```ada
>    X : Integer := Foo;
>    Y : Integer := Bar;
> 
>    X0 : constant Integer := X with Ghost;
>    Y0 : constant Integer := Y with Ghost;
> begin
>    declare
>       Tmp : Integer;
>    begin
>       pragma Assert (Y = Y0 and X = X0);
>    
>       Tmp := X;
> 
>       pragma Assert (Y = Y0 and Tmp = X0);
> 
>       X := Y;
> 
>       pragma Assert (X = Y0 and Tmp = X0);
> 
>       Y := Tmp;
>    end;
> 
>    pragma Assert (X = Y0 and Y = X0);
> ```

{pause up}
### Another Hoare logic example

{carousel change-page=~n:all}
> ```ada
> …
>    X : Modular_Integer := Foo (…);
>    Y : Modular_Integer := Bar (…);
> 
>    X0 : constant Modular_Integer := X with Ghost;
>    Y0 : constant Modular_Integer := Y with Ghost;
> begin
>    X := X xor Y;
>    Y := Y xor X;
>    X := X xor Y;
> 
>    pragma Assert (X = Y0 and Y = X0);
> …
> ```
> 
> {style="font-size:28px"}
> ```ada
> …
>    X : Modular_Integer := Foo (…);
>    Y : Modular_Integer := Bar (…);
> 
>    X0 : constant Modular_Integer := X with Ghost;
>    Y0 : constant Modular_Integer := Y with Ghost;
> begin
>    pragma Assert (X = X0 and Y = Y0);
> 
>    X := X xor Y;
> 
>    pragma Assert (X = (X0 xor Y0) and Y = Y0);
> 
>    Y := Y xor X;
> 
>    pragma Assert (X = (X0 xor Y0) and Y = (Y0 xor X0 xor Y0));
>    pragma Assert (X = (X0 xor Y0) and Y = X0);
> 
>    X := X xor Y;
> 
>    pragma Assert (X = (X0 xor Y0 xor X0) and Y = X0);
>    pragma Assert (X = Y0 and Y = X0);
> …
> ```

{pause up}
### An attempt to add pointers

```ada
…
   -- Not valid SPARK!
   X : constant access Modular_Integer := Foo (…);
   Y : constant access Modular_Integer := Bar (…);

   X0 : constant Modular_Integer := X.all with Ghost;
   Y0 : constant Modular_Integer := Y.all with Ghost;
begin
   X.all := X.all xor Y.all;
   Y.all := Y.all xor X.all;
   X.all := X.all xor Y.all;

   -- Wrong!
   pragma Assert (X.all = Y0 and Y.all = X0);
…
```

{pause up}
